# THE OWNER'S FILES (review of #2873, 2026-11-01). A migration that is not plainly additive is applied
# only once the owner approves it, by a committed line in the approvals file; the four others decide
# what that line means - the judge, the loop that asks it, the workflow that refuses to arm a pull
# request touching any of these, and this file. `arm-auto-merge.yml` never arms such a pull request;
# with the ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners" ticked, GitHub also refuses to merge one
# without the owner's review, however it was armed. The list below is the workflow's, line for line
# (`.github/scripts/tests/arm-auto-merge-app.test.sh` B32). Mechanism: docs/wiki/cicd.md.
/infrastructure/migration-approvals.txt @DeMASKe
/infrastructure/lib/migration-hold.sh @DeMASKe
/infrastructure/lib/migrations.sh @DeMASKe
/.github/workflows/arm-auto-merge.yml @DeMASKe
/.github/CODEOWNERS @DeMASKe
